desktop-shell-workspace-window-bar(1)

# NAME

desktop-shell-workspace-window-bar - bar listing the windows of each workspace

# SYNOPSIS

*desktop-shell-workspace-window-bar* [*-c* _FILE_] [*-s* _FILE_]

# DESCRIPTION

*desktop-shell-workspace-window-bar* puts a bar along the bottom of every
output. It lists the windows of the workspace shown on that output as their
application name (the Wayland app ID or X11 class) and process ID. The
focused window is highlighted, and clicking a window focuses it.

The bar is exactly as tall as the space the compositor's top bar reserves,
so the two bars match. It follows the compositor through its IPC socket,
found in _$SWAYSOCK_, and exits when the compositor does. After a package
upgrade, *swaymsg reload* restarts it from the new file.

# OPTIONS

*-h, --help*
	Show the help message and exit.

*-c, --config* _FILE_
	Read settings from _FILE_ instead of the usual places.

*-s, --style* _FILE_
	Load _FILE_ instead of the shipped workspace-window-bar.css. The shared
	theme is still loaded first.

# CONFIGURATION

The installed _@sysconfdir@/sway/config.d/60-desktop-shell-workspace-window-bar.conf_
starts the bar with sway. A second copy started by a configuration reload exits
at once, so the line can safely be:

```
exec_always desktop-shell-workspace-window-bar
```

# SETTINGS

Read from _$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/desktop-shell-components/workspace-window-bar.ini_,
else _/etc/xdg/desktop-shell-components/workspace-window-bar.ini_, which lists
every setting with its default. All are optional; *swaymsg reload* applies
changes.

*[bar]*
	*enabled* = _true_|_false_ (false closes the bar)++
	*position* = _bottom_|_top_++
	*height* = _auto_|_10-200_ (auto matches sway's top bar)++
	*label* = text with *{name}* *{pid}* *{title}* *{workspace}*++
	*left-click*, *middle-click*, *right-click* = _focus_|_close_|_menu_|_nothing_ (menu: the window menu, see *desktop-shell-window-context-menu*(1))

*[appearance]*
	*follow-sway-bar* = _true_|_false_

# STYLING

Without any style sheet the program takes its colors and font from the sway
bar, or from the GTK theme when there is no bar or *follow-sway-bar* is
false. Style sheets load in this order, each overriding the ones before:
_@shared_data_directory@/shared-theme.css_ and _@shared_data_directory@/workspace-window-bar.css_
(or the *--style* file), then the same two names in
_/etc/xdg/desktop-shell-components_, then in
_$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/desktop-shell-components_.

Colors are the CSS variables *--theme-background-color*, *--theme-text-color*,
*--theme-secondary-text-color*, *--theme-accent-color*,
*--theme-accent-text-color*, *--theme-border-color* and *--theme-urgent-color*.

The window has the _workspace-window-bar_ class. Each window is a button with
the _workspace-window-bar-entry_ class, plus _focused-window_ for the focused
one.

# SEE ALSO

*sway*(5), *sway-bar*(5), *sway-ipc*(7), *desktop-shell-window-switcher*(1)
